# Title Review Module

> Verify mineral ownership, identify title defects, and prepare acquisitions for closing.

---

# Overview

The Title Review module manages the legal examination of mineral ownership after a Purchase & Sale Agreement (PSA) has been executed.

Its purpose is to confirm ownership, identify title defects, determine curative requirements, and ensure each acquisition is legally ready to close.

This module serves as the bridge between PSA execution and Closing.

---

# Objectives

The Title Review module enables users to:

- Verify mineral ownership
- Examine chain of title
- Review probate records
- Identify ownership discrepancies
- Track title defects
- Request curative documents
- Prepare assets for closing
- Maintain legal audit history

---

# Key Features

## Ownership Verification

Verify:

- Grantor
- Grantee
- Current Owner
- Heirs
- Trusts
- Estates

---

## Chain of Title Review

Track ownership transfers including:

- Deeds
- Assignments
- Probate
- Affidavits
- Court Orders
- Divorce Decrees

---

## Mineral Interest Verification

Review

- Net Mineral Acres (NMA)
- Royalty Interest (RI)
- Working Interest (WI)
- Decimal Interest
- Ownership Percentages

---

## Title Defect Tracking

Examples include:

- Missing Deed
- Probate Required
- Incorrect Legal Description
- Unsigned PSA
- Trust Documentation
- Missing Division Order
- Incorrect Ownership
- Affidavit Required

